## 1) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Test
Title: Fix test cleanup so it removes the IDPs the test created

Affected:
- testsuite/integration-arquillian/tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/organization/cache/OrganizationCacheTest.java:381-381
- testsuite/integration-arquillian/tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/organization/cache/OrganizationCacheTest.java:425-425

Explanation:
The cleanup is registered as `testRealm().identityProviders().get("alias")::remove`. That uses the literal string `"alias"`, not the alias of the IDP that was just created.

As a result, none of the 21 IDPs (`idp-alias-0` … `idp-alias-20`) are removed after the test. They stay in the realm and are still linked to the organization. Later tests that count IDPs or depend on organization/IDP state can become flaky or fail.

Proposed fix:
~~~java
String alias = "idp-alias-" + i;
idpRep.setAlias(alias);
...
testRealm().identityProviders().create(idpRep).close();
getCleanup().addCleanup(testRealm().identityProviders().get(alias)::remove);
~~~
Apply the same change at line 425, using `"idp-alias-20"`.

## 2) Severity: MEDIUM | Type: Bug
Title: Invalidate login IDP cache when organization state changes, not only on IDP updates

Affected:
- model/infinispan/src/main/java/org/keycloak/models/cache/infinispan/idp/InfinispanIdentityProviderStorageProvider.java:213-255
- services/src/main/java/org/keycloak/organization/forms/login/freemarker/model/OrganizationAwareIdentityProviderBean.java:75-80

Explanation:
The new login cache stores IDP IDs. It is invalidated only by IDP create, update, or remove through this provider.

Whether an org-linked IDP is usable for login also depends on its organization. For example, disabling an organization makes its IDPs effectively disabled; this is why the bean now re-checks `isEnabled()` on the wrapped model. Organization enable/disable, and possibly organization removal (depending on how IDPs are unlinked, which is outside this diff), never invalidate `cacheKeyForLogin`. Stale IDs therefore stay cached.

The re-check of `isEnabled()` was added only in `OrganizationAwareIdentityProviderBean`. Any other caller of `getForLogin` that trusts the result (for example, the non-org `IdentityProviderBean`, redirectors, or custom extensions; outside this diff) may now get IDPs belonging to disabled organizations. Before this change, the delegate's query would have filtered those out.

Either invalidate the login caches from the organization cache provider on organization update/remove, or filter `isEnabled()` (on the wrapped model) inside `getForLogin` itself so all callers get correct results.

Proposed fix:
~~~java
// in getForLogin, when materializing cached ids:
IdentityProviderModel idp = session.identityProviders().getById(id);
if (idp == null) { ... }
if (idp.isEnabled()) {
    identityProviders.add(idp);
}
// and/or in InfinispanOrganizationProvider.update/remove:
for (FetchMode mode : FetchMode.values()) {
    realmCache.registerInvalidation(InfinispanIdentityProviderStorageProvider.cacheKeyForLogin(realm, mode));
}
~~~

## 3) Severity: LOW | Type: Maintainability
Title: Check other callers of the shared SPI `getLoginPredicate()` after the semantic change

Affected:
- server-spi/src/main/java/org/keycloak/models/IdentityProviderStorageProvider.java:254-254

Explanation:
`getLoginPredicate()` is a public static helper in the SPI. It now also requires `BROKER_PUBLIC=true` for any org-linked IDP.

This change was made to support cache-invalidation decisions, but it affects every existing consumer of the predicate. One example would be the JPA provider or other code building login filters, which is outside this diff. Such consumers could silently start excluding non-public org IDPs, for instance when they evaluate IDPs for a specific organization where non-public brokers were intended to be included.

Verify all usages. If the extra condition is only needed for invalidation, keep it in a private helper in the Infinispan provider instead of changing the SPI contract.

Proposed fix:
~~~java
// InfinispanIdentityProviderStorageProvider
private static final Predicate<IdentityProviderModel> LOGIN_CACHE_PREDICATE =
    getLoginPredicate().and(idp -> idp.getOrganizationId() == null
        || Boolean.parseBoolean(idp.getConfig().get(OrganizationModel.BROKER_PUBLIC)));
~~~
